Feature: Load and Validate Data into purgo_playground.f_invntry_bal_dly_hist

  Background:
    Given the source tables are available in purgo_databricks.purgo_playground
      | Table Name                  |
      | itemledgerentrieswopd       |
      | sap_master_data             |
      | item_qty_on_hand            |
      | reservation_entry           |
      | Itemwopd                    |
    And the target table purgo_playground.f_invntry_bal_dly_hist is defined
    And the necessary permissions are configured in the Unity Catalog purgo_databricks

  Scenario: Successfully load a complete and valid record
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | item_no_    | "ITEM123"               |
      | location_code | "HAUPT"                |
      | posting_date | "2023-10-01"            |
      | reservation_status | "0"               |
      | source_type | "37"                    |
      | expiration_date | "2024-12-31"         |
      | serial_no_ | "SN12345"                |
      | lot_no_    | "LOT67890"               |
      | qty_on_hand | "100.50"                |
      | quantity_base | "-50.25"              |
      | quantity_mrp_nettable | "80.00"      |
      | standard_cost | "25.75"               |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then a record should be inserted into f_invntry_bal_dly_hist with:
      | co_key                        | "nav_ger1050"                                 |
      | g_account                     | "ACC12345"                                    |
      | g_assignment_type             | "Account"                                     |
      | g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd         | "<current_date>"                              |
      | g_company_cd                  | "1050"                                        |
      | g_company_currency_cd         | "EUR"                                         |
      | g_dnsa_dt_yyyymmdd            | "2024-12-31"                                  |
      | g_expiration_dt_yyyymmdd      | "99991231"                                    |
      | g_item_nbr                    | "ITEM123"                                     |
      | g_location_cd                 | "HAUPT"                                       |
      | g_location_status_cd          | "none"                                        |
      | g_lot_effective_dt_yyyymmdd   | "19000101"                                    |
      | g_lot_nbr                     | "LOT67890"                                    |
      | g_lot_status_cd               | "none"                                        |
      | g_plant_cd                    | "CAGER"                                       |
      | g_qty_allocated               | "50.25"                                       |
      | g_qty_available               | "100.50"                                      |
      | g_qty_financial_nettable      | "100.50"                                      |
      | g_qty_in_transit              | null                                          |
      | g_qty_mrp_nettable            | "80.00"                                       |
      | g_qty_on_hand                 | "100.50"                                      |
      | g_qty_shippable               | "100.50"                                      |
      | g_source_system_cd            | "nav_ger"                                     |
      | g_unit_cost_company_currency  | "25.75"                                       |
      | plant_key                     | "nav_gerCAGER"                                |
      | plant_location_key            | "nav_gerCAGERHAUPT"                           |
      | prod_key                      | "nav_gerITEM123"                              |
      | prod_plant_key                | "nav_gerITEM123CAGER"                         |
      | prod_plant_location_key       | "nav_gerITEM123CAGERHAUPT"                    |
      | prod_plant_lot_key            | "nav_gerITEM123CAGERLOT67890"                 |
      | prod_plant_lot_location_key   | "nav_gerITEM123CAGERLOT67890HAUPT"            |

  Scenario Outline: Validate default and hardcoded field values when source data is missing
    Given the source table itemledgerentrieswopd has a record with:
      | item_no_    | "<item_no_>"            |
      | location_code | "<location_code>"     |
      | posting_date | "<posting_date>"      |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have:
      | g_assignment_type           | "Account"                             |
      | g_company_cd                | "1050"                                |
      | g_company_currency_cd       | "EUR"                                 |
      | g_location_status_cd        | "none"                                |
      | g_lot_status_cd             | "none"                                |
      | g_plant_cd                  | "CAGER"                               |
      | g_source_system_cd          | "nav_ger"                             |
      | g_qty_in_transit            | null                                  |
    Examples:
      | item_no_ | location_code | posting_date |
      | "ITEM456"| "GERMERING"   | "2023-09-15"  |
      | "ITEM789"| "LIN"         | "2023-08-20"  |

  Scenario: Fail to load record with missing mandatory field g_account
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | item_no_    | "ITEM123"               |
      | location_code | "HAUPT"                |
      | posting_date | "2023-10-01"            |
      | reservation_status | "0"               |
      | source_type | "37"                    |
      | expiration_date | "2024-12-31"         |
      | serial_no_ | "SN12345"                |
      | lot_no_    | "LOT67890"               |
      | qty_on_hand | "100.50"                |
      | quantity_base | "-50.25"              |
      | quantity_mrp_nettable | "80.00"      |
      | standard_cost | "25.75"               |
    And the g_account field is missing
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the record should not be inserted
    And an error "g_account is missing or invalid" should be logged

  Scenario: Validate alphanumeric constraint on g_account
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | item_no_    | "ITEM123"               |
      | location_code | "HAUPT"                |
      | posting_date | "2023-10-01"            |
      | reservation_status | "0"               |
      | source_type | "37"                    |
      | expiration_date | "2024-12-31"         |
      | serial_no_ | "SN12345"                |
      | lot_no_    | "LOT67890"               |
      | qty_on_hand | "100.50"                |
      | quantity_base | "-50.25"              |
      | quantity_mrp_nettable | "80.00"      |
      | standard_cost | "25.75"               |
      | g_account  | "ACC@123"                |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the record should not be inserted
    And an error "g_account must be alphanumeric" should be logged

  Scenario: Validate date format for g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | item_no_    | "ITEM123"               |
      | location_code | "HAUPT"                |
      | posting_date | "2023-10-01"            |
      | reservation_status | "0"               |
      | source_type | "37"                    |
      | expiration_date | "2024-12-31"         |
      | serial_no_ | "SN12345"                |
      | lot_no_    | "LOT67890"               |
      | qty_on_hand | "100.50"                |
      | quantity_base | "-50.25"              |
      | quantity_mrp_nettable | "80.00"      |
      | standard_cost | "25.75"               |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd in "YYYYMMDD" format

  Scenario: Validate concatenation for plant_key
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | source_system_cd | "nav_ger"             |
      | g_plant_cd       | "CAGER"               |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have plant_key as "nav_gerCAGER"

  Scenario: Validate conditional population of g_qty_allocated
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | quantity_base | "-50.25"              |
      | item_no_      | "ITEM123"             |
      | location_code | "HAUPT"               |
      | serial_no_    | "SN12345"             |
      | lot_no_       | "LOT67890"            |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_qty_allocated as "50.25"

  Scenario Outline: Validate g_qty_available based on location_code
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | qty_on_hand    | "<qty_on_hand>"    |
      | location_code  | "<location_code>"  |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_qty_available as "<expected_qty_available>"
    Examples:
      | qty_on_hand | location_code | expected_qty_available |
      | "100.50"    | "HAUPT"        | "100.50"               |
      | "200.00"    | "GERMERING"    | "200.00"               |
      | "150.75"    | "OTHER"        | null                   |

  Scenario Outline: Validate g_qty_mrp_nettable based on location_code
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | qty_on_hand    | "<qty_on_hand>"                  |
      | location_code  | "<location_code>"                |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_qty_mrp_nettable as "<expected_qty_mrp_nettable>"
    Examples:
      | qty_on_hand | location_code | expected_qty_mrp_nettable |
      | "80.00"     | "HAUPT"        | "80.00"                   |
      | "60.50"     | "QS-WE"        | "60.50"                   |
      | "70.25"     | "AH-LOC"       | "70.25"                   |
      | "90.00"     | "UNKNOWN"      | null                      |

  Scenario: Validate hardcoded value for g_source_system_cd
    Given the source tables contain a record
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_source_system_cd as "nav_ger"

  Scenario: Validate NULL handling for g_qty_in_transit
    Given the source tables contain a record
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_qty_in_transit as null

  Scenario: Validate default value for g_assignment_type when not represented
    Given the source tables contain a record without g_assignment_type
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_assignment_type as "Account"

  Scenario: Validate derived plant_location_key concatenation
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | source_system_cd | "nav_ger"         |
      | g_plant_cd       | "CAGER"           |
      | g_location_cd    | "HAUPT"           |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have plant_location_key as "nav_gerCAGERHAUPT"

  Scenario: Validate error logging for invalid data type in g_qty_on_hand
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | qty_on_hand | "invalid_decimal" |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the record should not be inserted
    And an error "g_qty_on_hand must be a decimal number" should be logged

  Scenario: Validate default value for g_lot_nbr when lot_no_ contains blank space
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | lot_no_ | "LOT 67890" |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_lot_nbr as "none"

  Scenario: Validate derived key prod_plant_lot_location_key
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | source_system_cd | "nav_ger"         |
      | g_item_nbr       | "ITEM123"         |
      | g_plant_cd       | "CAGER"           |
      | g_lot_nbr        | "LOT67890"        |
      | g_location_cd    | "HAUPT"           |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have prod_plant_lot_location_key as "nav_gerITEM123CAGERLOT67890HAUPT"

  Scenario: Validate date completeness for g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd
    Given the source tables contain a record with current date
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_capture_dt_yyyymmdd as the current date in "YYYYMMDD" format

  Scenario: Validate handling of multiple joins without data duplication
    Given the source tables item_qty_on_hand, itemledgerentrieswopd, sap_master_data, reservation_entry, and Itemwopd contain related records
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the record count in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist should equal the driving table item_qty_on_hand record count
    And no duplicate records should exist in f_invntry_bal_dly_hist

  Scenario: Validate data quality rules enforcement for alphanumeric fields
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | g_account | "ACC123"       |
      | g_item_nbr | "ITEM456"     |
      | g_location_cd | "LOC789"    |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then all alphanumeric fields in the inserted record should contain only alphanumeric characters

  Scenario: Validate ISO 4217 compliance for g_company_currency_cd
    Given the source tables contain a record
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_company_currency_cd as a valid ISO 4217 currency code

  Scenario: Validate scheduling and automation of daily data processing
    Given the SQL-based logic is scheduled to run daily
    When the scheduled job executes
    Then the f_invntry_bal_dly_hist table should be updated with the latest 100 days of data

  Scenario: Validate handling of NULL values in specific fields
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | some_field | null          |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have the corresponding field set to NULL as specified

  Scenario: Validate error handling and logging for SQL execution failures
    Given the source tables contain invalid data causing SQL execution to fail
    When the SQL-based logic is executed
    Then the process should not insert any records
    And an error log entry with the message "SQL execution failed due to invalid data" should be created

  Scenario: Validate performance metrics are recorded after data load
    Given the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    When the data load completes
    Then performance metrics such as execution time and record count should be logged

  Scenario: Validate change management by version controlling SQL logic
    Given a new version of the SQL-based logic is committed to version control
    When the SQL-based logic is deployed
    Then the deployed version should match the version in the version control system

  Scenario: Validate security compliance by restricting access to the target table
    Given a user without proper permissions attempts to access f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    When the user queries the table
    Then access should be denied with a "Permission denied" error

  Scenario: Validate transformation logic for conditional quantity population
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | location_code | "MATRIUM"    |
      | qty_on_hand   | "300.00"     |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then the inserted record should have g_qty_available as "300.00"

  Scenario: Validate handling of derived fields with complex concatenation
    Given the source tables contain a record with:
      | source_system_cd | "nav_ger"       |
      | g_item_nbr       | "ITEM123"       |
      | g_plant_cd       | "CAGER"         |
      | g_location_cd    | "HAUPT"         |
      | g_lot_nbr        | "LOT67890"      |
    When the SQL-based logic is executed to populate f_invntry_bal_dly_hist
    Then all derived keys should be correctly concatenated as follows:
      | plant_key                   | "nav_gerCAGER"                     |
      | plant_location_key          | "nav_gerCAGERHAUPT"                |
      | prod_key                    | "nav_gerITEM123"                   |
      | prod_plant_key              | "nav_gerITEM123CAGER"              |
      | prod_plant_location_key     | "nav_gerITEM123CAGERHAUPT"         |
      | prod_plant_lot_key          | "nav_gerITEM123CAGERLOT67890"      |
      | prod_plant_lot_location_key | "nav_gerITEM123CAGERLOT67890HAUPT" |
